    "result_text": "All 51 tests pass, including the new Cp37 test. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived, human-readable `telephoneDisplay` field to the owner representation while leaving the raw `telephone` in E.164 form.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` and a `telephoneDisplay(Owner)` helper, following the same pattern as the other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `identityKey`, etc.). It splits the E.164 country code (single-digit for `+1`/NANP, two-digit otherwise \u2014 matching the app's own recognised country codes), then emits the country code, a space, and the national digits grouped in threes from the left. So the stored `+61412345678` renders as `+61 412 345 678`, and `telephone` stays untouched.\n\n`null`/non-E.164 values are returned unchanged for safety.\n\n**Verification:** `Cp37Tests.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` passes (`$.telephone` = `+61412345678`, `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`), and the full suite is green \u2014 **51 tests run, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
